{"name":"Hazelwood","hex":"#fff3d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hazelwood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A village and civil parish in Amber Valley district, Derbyshire, England ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hazelwood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hazelwood, Victoria","blocks":[{"text":"Hazelwood is an area of Gippsland at the foot of the Strzelecki Ranges in Victoria, Australia. In the beginning the area acted as a service centre for the Hazelwood Power Station. Following the death of Sir Winston Churchill the town centre was renamed to Churchill, however many of the surrounding areas continue to carry the name Hazelwood."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazelwood%2C_Victoria","wikidata":"Q5688152"},{"title":"Hazelwood Power Station","blocks":[{"text":"The Hazelwood Power Station is a decommissioned brown-coal fuelled thermal power station located in the Latrobe Valley of Victoria, Australia. Built between 1964 and 1971, the 1,600-megawatt-capacity power station was made up of eight 200MW units, and supplied up to 25% of Victoria's base load electricity and more than 5% of Australia's total electricity demand. It was a 'subcritical' pulverized coal-fired boiler. The station was listed as the least carbon efficient power station in the OECD in a 2005 report by WWF Australia, making it one of the most polluting power stations in the world. At 1.56 tonnes of CO2 for each megawatt hour of electricity, it was 50% more polluting than the average black-coal power station in New South Wales or Queensland. Hazelwood emitted 14% of Victoria's annual greenhouse gas emissions and 3% of Australia's greenhouse gas emissions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Hazelwood_Power_Station.jpg/330px-Hazelwood_Power_Station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazelwood_Power_Station","wikidata":"Q1786119"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/LaTrobe_Valley_CFPS.png/500px-LaTrobe_Valley_CFPS.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/LaTrobe_Valley_CFPS.png/500px-LaTrobe_Valley_CFPS.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of the major towns and coal-fired power stations in the Latrobe Valley","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaTrobe_Valley_CFPS.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Hazelwoodpowerstationatnight.jpg/500px-Hazelwoodpowerstationatnight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Hazelwoodpowerstationatnight.jpg/1280px-Hazelwoodpowerstationatnight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Hazelwoodpowerstationatnight.jpg/500px-Hazelwoodpowerstationatnight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hazelwood Power Station at night in 2016","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHazelwoodpowerstationatnight.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Hazelwood_Power_Station_Closure_1.jpg/500px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_Closure_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Hazelwood_Power_Station_Closure_1.jpg/1280px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_Closure_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Hazelwood_Power_Station_Closure_1.jpg/500px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_Closure_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hazelwood shutting down Unit 1 for the last time on 29 March 2017. The thick plume of smoke is caused by a combination of the electrostatic precipitators switching off automatically during the shut down to eliminate the risk of them igniting, and what's left of the auxiliary fuel (briquettes) stored on site being fed into the boiler to empty their stores.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHazelwood_Power_Station_Closure_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Hazelwood_Power_Station_Pollution.jpg/500px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_Pollution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Hazelwood_Power_Station_Pollution.jpg/1280px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_Pollution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Hazelwood_Power_Station_Pollution.jpg/500px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_Pollution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Unit number three is coming back online following a shut down, resulting in a plume of visible smoke due to the electrostatic precipitators being offline for the duration of the start-up.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHazelwood_Power_Station_Pollution.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Hazelwood_Power_Station_seen_from_the_air.jpg/500px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_seen_from_the_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Hazelwood_Power_Station_seen_from_the_air.jpg/1280px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_seen_from_the_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Hazelwood_Power_Station_seen_from_the_air.jpg/500px-Hazelwood_Power_Station_seen_from_the_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hazelwood Power Station as seen from an aircraft in 2009.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHazelwood_Power_Station_seen_from_the_air.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Civil_disobedience_rally_at_Hazelwood_September_2009.jpg/500px-Civil_disobedience_rally_at_Hazelwood_September_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Civil_disobedience_rally_at_Hazelwood_September_2009.jpg/500px-Civil_disobedience_rally_at_Hazelwood_September_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"500 people symbolically decommissioned the developed world's dirtiest power station at the \"Switch off coal, switch on renewables\" event in September 2009.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACivil_disobedience_rally_at_Hazelwood_September_2009.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Human_made_solar_thermal_plant_hazelwood_victoria.JPG/500px-Human_made_solar_thermal_plant_hazelwood_victoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Human_made_solar_thermal_plant_hazelwood_victoria.JPG/1280px-Human_made_solar_thermal_plant_hazelwood_victoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Human_made_solar_thermal_plant_hazelwood_victoria.JPG/500px-Human_made_solar_thermal_plant_hazelwood_victoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The replica Solar Thermal plant at the 2010 rally.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuman_made_solar_thermal_plant_hazelwood_victoria.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Rally_Octo